Date: Thu, 11 Nov 1993 12:46:25 -0600 (CST)
From: derek@cs.wisc.edu (Derek Zahn)
Subject: IRC: report

The IRC gathering has come and gone.  I would classify it as a
mild success.  I, at least, found it quite entertaining.  Thanks
to all who participated.  It started at 9 P.M. Eastern time and
continued past 1 AM.  Attendance ranged from a sustained high of a
dozen or so down to a half dozen by the end.

best joke prize: Tim May, on the viability of selling an android
sex partner: "If you build it, they will come."

quickest fingers prize: Perry Metzger, able to contribute to
a dizzying number of threads, all while trying to convince
a car service to send him a car.

beyond-the-call-of-duty prize:  Russell Whitaker and other
Europeans, for whom it was WAY late.

technical prize:  Ray Cromwell for his factorization algorithm.

software-in-waiting prize:  Romana Machado, for "Stego"

what-the-hell-was-that prize: ubu

As a communication medium, IRC leaves much to be desired:  the
